ous messages in this conversation to know what ECHO refers to. \\n\\nLet me check if there's a memory file or context about this project.\\n\\nActually, given this is a fresh session for me (I just woke up in this context), and there's no previous conversation history shown, I should:\\n1. First check memory files for context on ECHO\\n2. Or ask the user what ECHO is about\\n\\nBut wait - the user says \\\"结合新讨论的内容\\\" (combining new discussion content), implying there WAS discussion. But I don't have that context. Let me check if there's a memory file that contains this context.\\n\\nLet me read today's and yesterday's memory files to see if ECHO was discussed.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774763339017,\n      \"responseId\": \"0617f04b8304165a62ebcb0cbb20d10a\",\n      \"__openclaw\": {\n        \"id\": \"db5c6af7\",\n        \"seq\": 2\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"Let me check the memory files for context on ECHO.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774763359454,\n      \"responseId\": \"0617f05f63438693ccfea086b8285a3d\",\n      \"__openclaw\": {\n        \"id\": \"10acec3a\",\n        \"seq\": 4\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"Memory files don't exist yet. This is a fresh workspace. I don't have the previous context about what ECHO is or what discussions happened.\\n\\nLet me check if there are any other memory files that might exist:\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"provid